    "explanation": "Both of you: this dispute is about the $5.00 waiting-time fee on trip TRP-02740, and that fee cannot stand. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02740) shows a waiting_time_fee line of $5.00, a cancellation_fee line of $0.00 and a total_charged of $33.23, with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00; the $5.00 is the contested amount, and it is the only charge in issue. / POL-NS-10(d) makes a waiting-time fee chargeable only where the trip was completed and the driver's in-geofence dwell before the rider boarded, measured as POL-NS-01(c) measures it, exceeded the free waiting period in force. The free waiting period for this trip is 180 seconds, read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec (EV-TRIP-02740). The driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-02740), which is complete (100.0% coverage, 10-second sampling, no gaps), shows a single continuous in-geofence run from 09:11:59 to 09:13:39 - 100 seconds - because the driver left the geofence when the trip started at 09:13:39. The shortfall against the 180-second minimum is 80 seconds. The platform's own wait timer began at 09:12:01 (EV-TRIP-02740) but the driver did not hold position for the period the timer measured. POL-NS-10(e) therefore requires the unsupported waiting-time line to be refunded in full: $5.00 back to the rider. The independent POL-NS-06 shortfall argument and the POL-NS-01(c) dwell argument run to the same figure and are accepted. / Both advocates' points on the arrival marker are accepted: the marker is a driver BUTTON press, so POL-NS-12 does not apply and the exported trace governs (EV-TRIP-02740, EV-GPS-02740); and the tap was made with the driver at the pin, inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, so the marker is not false under POL-NS-05 and no false-arrival referral is produced by that clause. / On the driver's side, no compensation is due. POL-NS-01 does not apply in full: limb (d) requires the trip to be terminated by the driver with a no-show reason code, but this trip was completed normally at 09:43:59 with cancellation_reason_code null and cancelled_by null (EV-TRIP-02740), and no cancellation fee was charged on the ledger. POL-NS-07 has nothing to pay out for that reason. The anti-farming check is nevertheless not tripped (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d 0, completed_trips_30d 67), and no POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is engaged (rider no_show_disputes_30d 0 and disputes_with_counterparty_90d 0 on both profiles), so the case is decidable on the record. / The rider's POL-NS-04 arguments (the coordinating message 'coming' at 09:12:19, unanswered, with no in-app call, and the rider's device within the 100 m STANDARD presence radius) point the same way, but the refund here flows from POL-NS-10(e). The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02740-01 is absent from the record; no accumulation of separate in-geofence intervals is required because only one interval exists, so the advisory does not affect the outcome in either direction. No clause produces a referral or an escalation on these facts. Confidence is 0.95, within the cap of 1.0 set by the artifacts that carry the deciding dwell fact (EV-GPS-02740 and EV-TRIP-02740, each at weight 1.0)."
